+name=README_AUTONOMY_RUNBOOK.md
+contents:
+This runbook describes how the autonomous promotion and continuous-learning stacks operate, the human approval exceptions, and how to audit them.
+
+1) Overview
+ - The continuous-learning pipeline (ops/tekton/pipelines/continuous_learning_pipeline.yaml) runs retrain, validate, canary and policy-decision tasks.
+ - OPA policies determine whether a run can be auto-promoted. For `risk_class == "legal"` or if OPA returns `require_legal=true`, a legal/regulatory approval request is created and human intervention is required.
+ - Routine human approvals are removed for policy-permitted changes; only legal/regulatory or explicitly high-risk promotions require humans.
+
+2) How to enable auto-promotion gates
+ - Review and update OPA policies (services/decisioning/opa_slo_policies.rego and data) to encode risk thresholds.
+ - When ready, run the CI workflow `ops/ci/promote_autonomy_gates.yml` and provide manual confirmation "I_APPROVE".
+ - This will apply Gatekeeper constraints and webhook validation (cosign requirement).
+
+3) Evidence & Auditing
+ - All promotions, decisions, signatures and remediation attempts are uploaded to EVIDENCE_BUCKET (S3). Compliance reports are created by services/compliance/audit_collector.py.
+ - Audit reports are cosign-signed if cosign key is present and uploaded to `${EVIDENCE_BUCKET}/audits/`.
+
+4) Legal/regulatory exception workflow
+ - OPA should set `require_legal=true` for promotions that need legal review.
+ - The pipeline will create an approval request via the Approval API; legal team processes the request via Approval UI.
+ - Once legal approves, approval service triggers the promote task (or auto-promote controller will observe the approval and proceed).
+
+5) Safety & remediation
+ - Automated remediation (services/failure/remediation_engine.py) retries, restarts and resubmits pipelines. If remediation attempts exceed limit, an escalation request is created.
+ - Remediation tracker evidence is stored under `${EVIDENCE_BUCKET}/remediation/`.
+
+6) Long-term reliability proof
+ - services/reliability/long_term_monitor.py collects SLO samples and writes periodic reports to `${EVIDENCE_BUCKET}/reliability/`.
+ - Keep retention policies and archival processes to satisfy auditors.
+
+7) Keys, secrets & signing
+ - Keep cosign private key in KMS/Secret Manager. Use terraform/ops/cosign_kms_key.tf as an example to provision a KMS key.
+ - Ensure signer deployment is restricted to an Ops role; apply least-privilege via Terraform.
+
+8) Operational playbooks
